{"repositoryId":1285240829,"availability":"available","full":"austin-putz/tidybreed","name":"tidybreed","description":"R package for pipe-friendly breeding program simulation backed by DuckDB — larger-than-RAM genomic datasets, lazy evaluation, and tidy workflows.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-30T15:59:21Z","updated":"2026-10-14T02:22:30Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://austin-putz.github.io/tidybreed/","topics":[],"demo":"https://austin-putz.github.io/tidybreed/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:01.151Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:01.151Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:01.151Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T23:51:19.826Z","stars":3,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T02:46:01.151Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Breeding program simulation, backed by DuckDB, driven by dplyr.","tidybreed is very much in the \"alpha testing\" phase, I do not recommend building on it just yet. I am however looking for valuable feedback to finish the API prior to version 1.0.0","A pipe-friendly (%>% or |>) R package for breeding program simulation backed by DuckDB. Design large-scale genomic simulations without running out of memory — all data lives on disk in a DuckDB database and is queried lazily via dplyr."],"features":[":one: User identifies a table to pass via gettable()",":two: User filters/subsets the table to identify rows/records/animals",":three: User passes that table to either a define() function or add() function","add() :arrowright: functions often add data on individuals (e.g. TBV, EBV, Phenotype, Genotype, etc)",":four: New records are stored on disk to your .duckdb file (database)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/austin-putz/tidybreed/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"22c964ebc38b2167ed6895a37de5c5a1a1f7f1c6af3ffb895dd1f28f08aebc9a","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.032Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"20